# DEBT-0010 — Duplicated Context Compilation Logic (`build_prompt` vs `compile_context`)

**Status**: OPEN  
**Filed**: 2026-07-30  
**Priority**: Low  
**Category**: Duplicated Mechanisms / Architecture Drift  

---

## 1. Compromise
The live `AgentRuntime` adapter in [runtime/integrations/__init__.py](file:///Users/bob/GitHub/paeos/runtime/integrations/__init__.py) defines a custom `build_prompt(package: TaskPackage)` function to compile session prompts, duplicating prompt construction logic already present in [runtime/context_compiler.py](file:///Users/bob/GitHub/paeos/runtime/context_compiler.py) (`compile_context`).

## 2. Reason
B2.A introduced `ClaudeCodeRuntime` to interface directly with the Claude Code CLI. To quickly format task package fields (objective, write/read scopes, evidence obligations, matched scars) into a single CLI prompt string, `build_prompt` was implemented inline within `runtime/integrations/__init__.py`.

## 3. Ideal Solution
Refactor `ClaudeCodeRuntime` to consume `runtime.context_compiler.compile_context` directly as the single source of truth for context compilation (PAEOS-8 K5).

## 4. Repayment Conditions
Repay during Phase 3 runtime cleanup.

## 5. Estimated Impact
Low. Maintaining two separate prompt compilers creates a risk of desynchronization between context compilation specs and live worker session prompts.
